t/68-credential-thunk-errors.t:83-87 asserts the fetch updated entry shape
exactly:

  is \@updated, [
    { ref => $REFNAME, from => $HEX_OLD, to => $HEX_NEW },
    { ref => "refs/remotes/origin/topic", from => undef, to => $HEX_NEW },
  ], "...";

Ticket #16 unified the updated entry shape across fetch and push to the
four keys { ref, from, to, reason }, so update_tips now also emits
reason => "". Test2::V0 is() is an exact deep compare, so both expected
hashes now fail with [0]{reason} !exists / [1]{reason} !exists.

Fix (one line per hash, no logic change):

  { ref => $REFNAME, from => $HEX_OLD, to => $HEX_NEW, reason => "" },
  { ref => "refs/remotes/origin/topic", from => undef, to => $HEX_NEW, reason => "" },

NOT done in #16 because t/68 was outside that task file lock (three agents
working concurrently). The unification itself is pinned in
t/49-remote-callbacks.t section 3b.

Second, optional: t/68 uses a real non-zero oid for the new tip, so it is
unaffected by the other half of #16 (an all-zero NEW tip now maps to
to => undef, meaning "ref deleted"). Adding a case for that here would be
a good sibling to the existing all-zero OLD tip case.
